Hi Gleki,

I am a beginner in Lojban and I found your Introduction very motivational!
I read Lojban for Beginners and am reading the Wave Lessons, but what they 
lack is a practical take on the language.
I don't know how a more practical, even standard-textbook approach, could 
conflict with the more complex concepts,
but I find that the step to using the language is not decreasing if I 
*just* learn all the metaphysical grammar implications.
Your Introduction however takes a good step at reducing complexity to 
increase usability.

I would love reading more, wouldn't mind also some short exercises similar 
to L4B and WL.
This would really help increasing the active lojban-speaking community, I 
think.

Best wishes,
Davjd

